 "history": "With a petticoat, a jacket was the commonest working dress of the 1750s: fitted over the stays, pinned edge to edge, sleeves to the elbow, in worsted, linen or printed cotton, striped stuffs common (the Fort Ticonderoga guidelines) [S6]. The loose Pennsylvania German shortgown belongs to the later decades and is not used for 1757 [S10][S9].",
